# The whole build context is uploaded to the daemon before the first
# instruction runs. A 2 GB .venv here is 2 GB of waiting on every build, and
# on Windows, where the context crosses a VM boundary, it is considerably
# worse than that.

.venv/
.venv-*/
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Runtime output, not build input. logs/ in particular is a volume at run time
# -- baking a copy into the image would be shadowed by the mount anyway.
logs/
.prometheus/
tmp-pg/

# Secrets never enter an image layer: anything COPYed is readable forever via
# `docker history`, even if a later layer deletes it. Compose reads .env from
# the host at run time and passes it in as environment instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ~10 MB of wav used by a host-side script for auditioning TTS voices.
voice_samples/

# Re-fetched during the build, so whatever is on this machine is irrelevant --
# and a fresh clone has no copy at all.
ops/vendor/

# Documentation, and the starter package's own single-service compose file.
*.md
mock_api/docker-compose.yml

# The mock API is built from its own context (./mock_api); it does not need the
# agent's source, and the agent's image does not need the mock API.
mock_api/
